{
  "id": "Compound::DB04843 - Gene::1129",
  "verbalization": "Mepenzolate is likely to interact with Chrm2 through a mechanism involving G-protein coupled receptors. The evidence suggests that Mepenzolate binds to Chrm1, which is involved in the activation of G-protein coupled acetylcholine or neurotransmitter receptors. These receptors, in turn, are part of the broader Muscarinic or Neurotransmitter receptor pathways, which are ultimately linked to Chrm2. The varying scores in the paths reflect the strength of the interactions, with Chrm1 serving as a central node in the network. The shared involvement of Chrm1 in multiple receptor activities implies a general role in signaling pathways that may be targeted by Mepenzolate. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Mepenzolate influences Chrm2 through the modulation of receptor activity, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
